Joined drill: real queue, ledger, trace and restore; mock payment provider

A. reconcile before resume (the runbook)
enqueue op-a-T-2001: QUEUED; backup taken
w1 claim=1 paid key=k-65ff20dd26, crashed before recording
  ledger SUBMITTED, provider rows=1, job LEASED
workers stopped; restore from backup: job QUEUED
  ledger rows=0, provider rows=1 (the provider is not restored)
reconcile before resume: recorded from provider -> ledger CONFIRMED
w2 claim=1: payment calls=0, ledger CONFIRMED, job DONE
late w1 complete claim=1: refused (the restore rewound claim numbers)
provider payments for key=1, replies=1, double payments=0
trace b9f0f691:
  backup      job.state=QUEUED
  w1 refund   claim=1 ledger.state=SUBMITTED provider.rows=1
  restore     job.state=QUEUED ledger.rows=0
  reconcile   result=recorded from provider
  w2 resume   claim=1 calls=0 ledger.state=CONFIRMED

B. no reconcile, provider honours the key
enqueue op-a-T-2001: QUEUED; backup taken
w1 claim=1 paid key=k-65ff20dd26, crashed before recording
  ledger SUBMITTED, provider rows=1, job LEASED
workers stopped; restore from backup: job QUEUED
  ledger rows=0, provider rows=1 (the provider is not restored)
no reconcile: resume straight after the restore
w2 claim=1: payment calls=1, ledger CONFIRMED, job DONE
late w1 complete claim=1: refused (the restore rewound claim numbers)
provider payments for key=1, replies=1, double payments=0
trace b9f0f691:
  backup      job.state=QUEUED
  w1 refund   claim=1 ledger.state=SUBMITTED provider.rows=1
  restore     job.state=QUEUED ledger.rows=0
  w2 resume   claim=1 calls=1 ledger.state=CONFIRMED

C. no reconcile, provider ignores the key
enqueue op-a-T-2001: QUEUED; backup taken
w1 claim=1 paid key=k-65ff20dd26, crashed before recording
  ledger SUBMITTED, provider rows=1, job LEASED
workers stopped; restore from backup: job QUEUED
  ledger rows=0, provider rows=1 (the provider is not restored)
no reconcile: resume straight after the restore
w2 claim=1: payment calls=1, ledger CONFIRMED, job DONE
late w1 complete claim=1: refused (the restore rewound claim numbers)
provider payments for key=2, replies=1, double payments=1
trace b9f0f691:
  backup      job.state=QUEUED
  w1 refund   claim=1 ledger.state=SUBMITTED provider.rows=1
  restore     job.state=QUEUED ledger.rows=0
